{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"dimming-grandiose-swift","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nOnce Jira returns a key, local persistence can still fail. The canonical label is the durable remote identity floor; the entity property is optional enrichment. Local confirmation must use RP-02 as the single identity owner.\n\n## Outcome\nAfter create returns a key, attach `rebar-id:<local_id>` first, attempt the optional property second, then persist known key and confirmation through the RP-02 facade. Any failure returns a typed known-key safety abort without remote deletion.\n\n## Plan\n1. Require RP-02 repository/lifecycle/recovery facade to be available; do not create a second binding writer.\n2. Apply the canonical label before any property or local confirmation. Treat property unsupported/permission failure as visible enrichment failure that cannot erase the label floor.\n3. Persist known key and confirmation through named `BindingStore` operations and their unit of work.\n4. If label or persistence fails, preserve key, pending/recovery evidence, remote issue, and exact terminal disposition.\n5. Execute later lifecycle intents only after their remote postcondition is proven.\n\n## Testing\nFault cuts after returned key, during label, property, known-key save, and confirmation assert remote containment, local bytes, and outcomes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The canonical label is attempted before optional property and local confirmation.\n- [ ] Unsupported or forbidden property remains visible and cannot remove a successful label.\n- [ ] Known key and confirmation persist only through the RP-02 `BindingStore` facade.\n- [ ] Every post-create failure reports the known key and retains recovery evidence.\n- [ ] No post-create failure deletes the remote issue.\n- [ ] Other lifecycle intents execute only after their remote postconditions are proven.\n\n## Out of scope\nWhole-pass crash/restart convergence, dependency release, and production create cutover.","id":"1cb3-d60c-0d32-4cfe","parent_id":"59b0-d1b9-ad94-4339","priority":1,"tags":["rp03","create","binding-store","tdd"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-03 S4 T2 — Contain returned creates and confirm through BindingStore"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787028338153268001,"uuid":"d2febd39-3e7b-498a-add8-524670561562"}